{
  "_comment": "Synthetic fixture for the CDict vocabulary type. Mirrors the layout juliac would emit for `struct CDict{V}; length::Int64; keys::Ptr{CString}; values::Ptr{V}; end` (JLWInterop) instantiated at V=Float64, with one @ccallable function borrowing a CDict{Float64} argument and one returning an owned one, plus the macro-emitted `jlw_free`/`jlw_free_strings` release entrypoints so the owning return is `:auto`, not `:mechanical`. `keys` points to length-prefixed `CString` elements (`struct CString; length::Int32; data::Ptr{UInt8}; end`, size 16, offsets 0/8) rather than NUL-terminated `Ptr{UInt8}`s. Field offsets (0, 8, 16, size 24) match juliac's actual ABI JSON for `CDict{Float64}` verbatim (no padding needed — all three fields are already 8-byte aligned in declaration order). The Python emitter must recognize the CDict shape (name + full 3-field shape: `length`/`keys`/`values`, `keys` a `Ptr{CString}`, `values` a pointer to a primitive in `pytypes`) and emit from_dict/as_dict helpers plus an owning-return convert-then-free-twice façade wrapper (jlw_free_strings for keys, then jlw_free for values).",
